   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "I am trying to fit a confirmatory MIRT model with six dimensions. The model is a graded response IRT mode. The results of model fit were as follows<div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">M2   df p     RMSEA   RMSEA_5 RMSEA_95     SRMSR       TLI       CFI\r\nstats 40852.32 2678 0 0.1690169 0.1674037 0.170296 0.2572462 0.4269607 0.4461929</span></span></span><br></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">indicating a model misfit.</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">This was not the case when fitting the same model with the same data using CFA.</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">How can I interpret this contradiction in the results?</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Lucida Console, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">In addition, I got this error message:</span></font></div><div>Error: Can&#39;t plot high dimensional solutions.<font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Lucida Console, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\"><br></span></font></div><div><br></div><div>When asking for plots.</div><div><br></div><div>How can I get the ICC and IIC for item in MIRT with high dimensional models?</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
