  {
   "id": "xWyYPTRbAQAJ",
   "from": "Preston Botter",
   "author": "69c59fb419f3f75e",
   "date": "2024-02-26T02:16:48Z",
   "subject": "Re: Fit statistics and Item plots in MIRT - Graded response",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">While FA and IRT models have fit statistics with similar (or the exact same) names, they are different fit indices with different population values and thus should be interpreted differently. That being said, I would expect model fit information to convey <i>similar </i>information (e.g., your MIRT TLI is 0.43, and I would not expect your CFA TLI to be something like 0.14 or 0.94). <br><div><br></div><div>P</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Sun, Feb 25, 2024 at 8:53 PM Oxana Rosca &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oxan...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div></div>"
    ],
